# Wallet instance demo

The normative text is the IT-Wallet Technical Specifications. Its reStructuredText rules apply only in that repository.

- User-facing copy is an Italian `msgid`. The English `msgstr` states the same fact and is compiled into `messages.mo`.
- Implement a specified check once. Do not change its strength unless the user asks.
- Revocation reads the Status List in the credential. Do not call a status assertion endpoint.
- A success message reports the outcome. It does not say that a status was updated.
- Example hostnames stay under `example.org`.
- Do not commit or push unless the user asks in this request.
- Change only the requested part.
